description: Rules for Next.js API route handlers
globs: "**/api/**/*.ts"
---

# API Route Rules
- Wrap entire handler in try/catch. Never let errors propagate unhandled.
- Return JSON always. Errors: { error: string, code: string } with HTTP status.
- Validate ALL inputs. Use Zod schemas for request body validation.
- Rate limit by IP (src/lib/rate-limit.ts). Check before processing.
- Access KV only through src/lib/storage.ts. Never import @vercel/kv directly.
- Log errors: console.error('[API /path] description:', error)
- POST /api/sessions: create session, KV 24h TTL.
- POST /api/sessions/[id]/feedback: transcript -> Claude -> JSON -> KV 7d TTL.
- /api/realtime: WebSocket relay browser <-> OpenAI Realtime. API key stays server-side.
